module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.GeneratorIndependence
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.SectionIdealCechPresheaf
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# The site of local presentations of a finite-type sheaf of ideals

Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site and `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` a sheaf of ideals. The proof of [Stacks, Tag 099E]
attaches to an object `U` and a finitely generated ideal `I ⊆ ℐ(U)` generating `ℐ|_U` the complex
of presheaves `K^•_{U,I} : U'/U ↦ K(𝒪(U'), I𝒪(U'))`, and then has to glue those complexes over
all `U`. The gluing is the only step of that proof which is not a construction on one slice, and
the obstruction to performing it is that the ideal `I` is a *choice*: the assignment
`U ↦ (𝒪(U), I_U)` is not functorial for any choice of `I_U`, because restriction does not carry a
chosen presentation to a chosen one.

This file removes the choice by enlarging the site. Its objects are the **local presentations**
of `ℐ`: pairs of an object `U` of `𝒞` and a finite family `f_1, …, f_r` of sections of `𝒪` over
`U` generating `ℐ|_U`. On that category the assignment "ring of sections together with the ideal
the family spans" *is* a functor into `Stacks.RingIdealSite.RingIdeal`, so
`Stacks.RingIdealSite.kComplexNat` pulls back to a complex of presheaves of modules with no
choice anywhere, and the gluing problem becomes the statement that the forgetful functor to `𝒞`
does not change the topos.

That statement is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDenseSubsite_idealPresForget`, and it is where
the two inputs of the source's argument enter:

* **cover-density** is the first move of the source's proof, "replace `𝒞` by the full subcategory
  of objects `U` such that `ℐ|_U` is generated by finitely many sections", in the form
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isCoverDense_ι_isFinitelyGeneratedOver_of_isFiniteType`: every
  object of `𝒞` is covered by objects carrying a presentation, and an object carrying a
  presentation is in the image of the forgetful functor;
* **local fullness** is the source's generator-independence hint, "if `I'` is a finitely
  generated ideal which also generates `ℐ|_U`, then there exists a covering `{U_j → U}` such that
  `I𝒪(U_j) = I'𝒪(U_j)`", in the form
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_sieve_sectionSpan_eq`: an arrow of `𝒞` between the bases of
  two presentations lifts to the presentation site above a covering sieve, namely above the sieve
  on which the two presentations span the same ideals of sections.

The forgetful functor is *faithful* outright — a morphism of presentations is an arrow of `𝒞`
together with a proposition — so local faithfulness is free, and the three conditions together
are exactly Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsDenseSubsite`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.spanAt`: the ideal of `𝒪(V)` spanned by the values, at an arrow
  `V ⟶ U`, of a finite family of sections of `𝒪` over `U`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IdealPres`: **a local presentation of `ℐ`** — an object `U` of
  `𝒞` together with a finite family of sections of `𝒪` over `U` generating `ℐ|_U`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IdealPres.Hom` and the category structure: a morphism is an arrow
  of the bases above which the two families span the same ideals of sections at every object.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealPresForget`: the forgetful functor to `𝒞`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.presIdeal`: the ideal a presentation spans over its own base, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealPresRingIdeal`: the functor into the rings with an ideal that
  it defines, with `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.presCechComplex` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.presCechAugmentation` the complex `K^•` of [Stacks, Tag 099D]
  pulled back along it — the choice-free model of the complex `K^•_{U,I}`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealPresOver`: the slice `𝒞/U` over the base of a presentation,
  read inside the presentation site by restricting the presentation.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isCoverDense_idealPresForget`: the forgetful functor is cover
  dense for a finite-type sheaf of ideals.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isLocallyFull_idealPresForget`: it is locally full.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDenseSubsite_idealPresForget`: **the presentation site is a
  dense subsite of `(𝒞, J)`.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealPresOver_comp_forget`: `𝒞/U ⟶ 𝒞` factors through the
  presentation site, on the nose.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealPresOver_op_comp_idealPresRingIdeal` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealPresOver_comp_rightOp`: **the tautological functor into the
  rings with an ideal restricts, along a presentation `(U, f)`, to
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.ringIdealFunctor` at `f` on the slice site over `U`** — so the
  complex `K^•` of the presentation site restricts to the complex `K^•_{U,I}` on the slice site
  over `U`.

## Implementation notes

The morphism condition is stated as

`∀ ⦃V⦄ (p : V ⟶ P.obj) (q : V ⟶ Q.obj), p ≫ base = q → spanAt P.gen p = spanAt Q.gen q`

rather than as an equation between the spans at `p` and at `p ≫ base`. The two are equivalent,
but in the stated form every use is discharged by substituting the hypothesis, so no object of a
slice category is ever rewritten and no `eqToHom` appears; in the other form each use carries the
associativity or unit isomorphism of `𝒞` through `CategoryTheory.Over.mk`.

`spanAt` is a `def` with an ascribed result type `Ideal (X.O.obj.obj (op V))` rather than the
literal `Ideal ((X.over U).O.obj.obj (op (Over.mk p)))` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sectionSpan` on the slice site. The two types are definitionally
equal — `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.over_O_obj_obj` is `rfl` — but only the ascription makes
the spans at two different bases `P.obj` and `Q.obj` unify, which the morphism condition needs.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached. [Stacks, Tag 099E] asserts the existence of a global map
`K → 𝒪` in `D(𝒪)` with a Čech identification over every object where `ℐ` is finitely generated;
this file constructs the site on which the complex of its proof is defined without a choice of
generators, not that map.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 099E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099E)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099D)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u v w

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

section SpanAt

variable {X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}}

/-- **The ideal of `𝒪(V)` spanned by the values of a finite family of sections of `𝒪` over `U`
at an arrow `p : V ⟶ U`.** This is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sectionSpan` on the slice site
over `U`, at the object `p`, with its type written as an ideal of `𝒪(V)`. -/
def spanAt {U : X.C} {r : ℕ}
    (gen : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over U).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}))
    {V : X.C} (p : V ⟶ U) : Ideal (X.O.obj.obj (op V)) :=
  Ideal.span (Set.range fun i ↦ globalSectionVal (gen i) (op (Over.mk p)))

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.spanAt gen p` is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sectionSpan gen`
on the slice site over `U`, at the object `p`. -/
theorem spanAt_eq_sectionSpan {U : X.C} {r : ℕ}
    (gen : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over U).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}))
    {V : X.C} (p : V ⟶ U) :
    spanAt gen p = sectionSpan (X := X.over U) gen (op (Over.mk p)) := rfl

/-- The image of the object `a : V ⟶ W` of `𝒞/W` under `CategoryTheory.Over.map p` is the
object `a ≫ p` of `𝒞/U`. -/
theorem overMap_obj_mk {U W V : X.C} (p : W ⟶ U) (a : V ⟶ W) :
    (Over.map p).obj (Over.mk a) = Over.mk (a ≫ p) := rfl

/-- **Restricting the base of a family of sections does not change the spans it produces**: the
span of `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.overGlobalSectionRestrict p ∘ gen` at `a` is the span of
`gen` at `a ≫ p`. -/
theorem spanAt_overGlobalSectionRestrict {U W : X.C} {r : ℕ}
    (gen : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over U).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}))
    (p : W ⟶ U) {V : X.C} (a : V ⟶ W) :
    spanAt (fun i ↦ overGlobalSectionRestrict p (gen i)) a = spanAt gen (a ≫ p) := by
  unfold spanAt
  exact congrArg Ideal.span (congrArg Set.range (funext fun i ↦
    globalSectionVal_overGlobalSectionRestrict p (gen i) (op (Over.mk a))))

/-- **Restriction carries the span at an arrow to the span at a composite.** This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sectionSpan_map_eq` on the slice site over `U`, read through
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.spanAt`. -/
theorem spanAt_comp {U : X.C} {r : ℕ}
    (gen : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over U).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}))
    {V V' : X.C} (b : V ⟶ U) (a : V' ⟶ V) :
    spanAt gen (a ≫ b) = Ideal.map (X.O.obj.map a.op).hom (spanAt gen b) :=
  sectionSpan_map_eq (X := X.over U) gen
    (Quiver.Hom.op (X := Over.mk (a ≫ b)) (Y := Over.mk b) (Over.homMk a rfl))

/-- **Restriction carries the span at the base to the span at a restricted base.** This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sectionSpan_map_eq` on the slice site over `U`, read through
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.spanAt`. -/
theorem spanAt_eq_map_spanAt {U : X.C} {r : ℕ}
    (gen : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over U).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}))
    {V : X.C} (p : V ⟶ U) :
    spanAt gen p = Ideal.map (X.O.obj.map p.op).hom (spanAt gen (𝟙 U)) :=
  sectionSpan_map_eq (X := X.over U) gen
    (Quiver.Hom.op (X := Over.mk p) (Y := Over.mk (𝟙 U)) (Over.homMk p (by simp)))

end SpanAt

section Objects

variable {X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}}
  (𝓘 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))

/-- **A local presentation of a sheaf of ideals `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪`**: an object `U` of the site together
with a finite family of sections of `𝒪` over `U` — equivalently, of global sections of the
structure sheaf of the slice site over `U` — generating `ℐ|_U`.

These are the pairs `(U, I)` of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 099E], with the finitely generated
ideal `I ⊆ ℐ(U)` presented by a chosen family of generators. -/
structure IdealPres where
  /-- The base object of the presentation. -/
  obj : X.C
  /-- The number of generators. -/
  r : ℕ
  /-- The generators, as global sections of the structure sheaf of the slice site. -/
  gen : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over obj).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w})
  /-- They generate `ℐ|_U`. -/
  spec : overIdeal 𝓘 obj = generatedIdealSheaf gen

end Objects

section Morphisms

variable {X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}}
  {𝓘 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))}

/-- **A morphism of local presentations**: an arrow of the base objects above which the two
families span the same ideal of sections at every object. -/
structure IdealPres.Hom (P Q : IdealPres 𝓘) where
  /-- The underlying arrow of base objects. -/
  base : P.obj ⟶ Q.obj
  /-- The two families span the same ideals of sections above `base`. -/
  spanAt_eq : ∀ ⦃V : X.C⦄ (p : V ⟶ P.obj) (q : V ⟶ Q.obj), p ≫ base = q →
    spanAt P.gen p = spanAt Q.gen q

/-- A morphism of local presentations is determined by its underlying arrow. -/
theorem IdealPres.Hom.ext' {P Q : IdealPres 𝓘} :
    ∀ {u t : IdealPres.Hom P Q}, u.base = t.base → u = t
  | ⟨_, _⟩, ⟨_, _⟩, rfl => rfl

/-- **The presentation site of a sheaf of ideals.** -/
instance IdealPres.category : Category.{v} (IdealPres 𝓘) where
  Hom P Q := IdealPres.Hom P Q
  id P := ⟨𝟙 P.obj, fun _ p q hq ↦ by rw [← hq, Category.comp_id]⟩
  comp {_ _ _} u t :=
    ⟨u.base ≫ t.base, fun _ p s hs ↦
      (u.spanAt_eq p (p ≫ u.base) rfl).trans
        (t.spanAt_eq (p ≫ u.base) s (by rw [← hs, Category.assoc]))⟩
  id_comp u := IdealPres.Hom.ext' (Category.id_comp u.base)
  comp_id u := IdealPres.Hom.ext' (Category.comp_id u.base)
  assoc u t s := IdealPres.Hom.ext' (Category.assoc u.base t.base s.base)

/-- The underlying arrow of the identity of a presentation is the identity of its base. -/
@[simp]
theorem IdealPres.id_base (P : IdealPres 𝓘) : IdealPres.Hom.base (𝟙 P) = 𝟙 P.obj := rfl

/-- The underlying arrow of a composite of morphisms of presentations is the composite of their
underlying arrows. -/
@[simp]
theorem IdealPres.comp_base {P Q R : IdealPres 𝓘} (u : P ⟶ Q) (t : Q ⟶ R) :
    IdealPres.Hom.base (u ≫ t) = u.base ≫ t.base := rfl

/-- **The restriction of a presentation along an arrow `p : T ⟶ P.obj` into its base**: the
presentation with base `T` whose generators are the restrictions of those of `P`. -/
def IdealPres.restrict (P : IdealPres 𝓘) {T : X.C} (p : T ⟶ P.obj) : IdealPres 𝓘 where
  obj := T
  r := P.r
  gen i := overGlobalSectionRestrict p (P.gen i)
  spec := overIdeal_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_overGlobalSectionRestrict 𝓘 p P.spec

/-- The base of the restriction of `P` along `p : T ⟶ P.obj` is `T`. -/
@[simp]
theorem IdealPres.restrict_obj (P : IdealPres 𝓘) {T : X.C} (p : T ⟶ P.obj) :
    (P.restrict p).obj = T := rfl

/-- The span of the generators of `P.restrict p` at `a` is the span of the generators of `P` at
`a ≫ p`. -/
theorem IdealPres.spanAt_restrict (P : IdealPres 𝓘) {T : X.C} (p : T ⟶ P.obj) {V : X.C}
    (a : V ⟶ T) : spanAt (P.restrict p).gen a = spanAt P.gen (a ≫ p) :=
  spanAt_overGlobalSectionRestrict P.gen p a

/-- **The projection of a restricted presentation onto the presentation it restricts.** -/
def IdealPres.restrictHom (P : IdealPres 𝓘) {T : X.C} (p : T ⟶ P.obj) : P.restrict p ⟶ P where
  base := p
  spanAt_eq _ a _ hq := hq ▸ P.spanAt_restrict p a

/-- The underlying arrow of `P.restrictHom p` is `p`. -/
@[simp]
theorem IdealPres.restrictHom_base (P : IdealPres 𝓘) {T : X.C} (p : T ⟶ P.obj) :
    IdealPres.Hom.base (P.restrictHom p) = p := rfl

end Morphisms

section Forget

variable {X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}}
  (𝓘 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))

/-- **The forgetful functor from the presentation site to the site**, remembering only the base
object of a presentation. -/
def idealPresForget : IdealPres 𝓘 ⥤ X.C where
  obj P := P.obj
  map u := u.base

/-- The forgetful functor sends a presentation to its base. -/
@[simp]
theorem idealPresForget_obj (P : IdealPres 𝓘) : (idealPresForget 𝓘).obj P = P.obj := rfl

/-- The forgetful functor sends a morphism of presentations to its underlying arrow. -/
@[simp]
theorem idealPresForget_map {P Q : IdealPres 𝓘} (u : P ⟶ Q) :
    (idealPresForget 𝓘).map u = u.base := rfl

/-- The forgetful functor from the presentation site is faithful. -/
instance faithful_idealPresForget : (idealPresForget 𝓘).Faithful where
  map_injective h := IdealPres.Hom.ext' h

end Forget

section DenseSubsite

variable {X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}}
  (𝓘 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))

/-- **Two presentations whose bases are joined by an arrow span the same ideals of sections above
a covering sieve of the source base.** This is the generator-independence hint of
[Stacks, Tag 099E] — "if `I'` is a finitely generated ideal which also generates `ℐ|_U`, then
there exists a covering `{U_j → U}` such that `I𝒪(U_j) = I'𝒪(U_j)`" — read on the slice site over
`P.obj`, where the generators of `P` and the restrictions of those of `Q` are two finite families
of global sections generating the same sheaf of ideals. -/
theorem exists_sieve_spanAt_eq (P Q : IdealPres 𝓘) (h : P.obj ⟶ Q.obj) :
    ∃ S : Sieve P.obj, S ∈ X.J P.obj ∧
      ∀ ⦃V : X.C⦄ (b : V ⟶ P.obj), S.arrows b → spanAt P.gen b = spanAt Q.gen (b ≫ h) := by
  classical
  let g : Fin Q.r → Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over P.obj).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}) :=
    fun i ↦ overGlobalSectionRestrict h (Q.gen i)
  have heq : generatedIdealSheaf P.gen = generatedIdealSheaf g :=
    P.spec.symm.trans (overIdeal_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_overGlobalSectionRestrict 𝓘 h Q.spec)
  let Sa : Sieve (Over.mk (𝟙 P.obj)) :=
    spanAgreementSieve (X := X.over P.obj) P.gen g (Over.mk (𝟙 P.obj))
  have hcov : Sa ∈ (X.over P.obj).J (Over.mk (𝟙 P.obj)) := by
    refine spanAgreementSieve_mem P.gen g _ (fun j ↦ ?_) (fun i ↦ ?_)
    · rw [heq]
      exact globalSectionVal_mem_generatedIdealSheaf g j _
    · rw [← heq]
      exact globalSectionVal_mem_generatedIdealSheaf P.gen i _
  refine ⟨Sieve.overEquiv (Over.mk (𝟙 P.obj)) Sa, hcov, fun V b hb ↦ ?_⟩
  have hb' := Sa.downward_closed ((Sieve.overEquiv_iff Sa b).1 hb)
    (Over.homMk (𝟙 V) (by simp) : Over.mk b ⟶ Over.mk (b ≫ 𝟙 P.obj))
  exact (sectionSpan_eq_of_mem_spanAgreementSieve P.gen g _ hb').trans
    (spanAt_overGlobalSectionRestrict Q.gen h b)

/-- **The forgetful functor from the presentation site is cover dense**, given a family of
objects covering the final object on each of which `ℐ` is generated by finitely many sections.
Every object of `𝒞` is covered by objects admitting a presentation — a presentation restricts
along every arrow, `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IdealPres.restrict` — and an object admitting a
presentation is the base of one. -/
theorem isCoverDense_idealPresForget {ι : Type*} {V : ι → X.C}
    (hV : X.J.CoversTop V) (hfg : ∀ i, IsFinitelyGeneratedOver 𝓘 (V i)) :
    (idealPresForget 𝓘).IsCoverDense X.J where
  is_cover U := by
    refine X.J.superset_covering (fun T p hp ↦ ?_) (hV U)
    obtain ⟨i, ⟨b⟩⟩ := (Sieve.mem_ofObjects_iff V p).1 hp
    obtain ⟨r, f, hf⟩ := hfg i
    exact ⟨⟨IdealPres.restrict ⟨V i, r, f, hf⟩ b, 𝟙 T, p, Category.id_comp p⟩⟩

/-- **The forgetful functor from the presentation site is locally full.** An arrow of `𝒞`
between the bases of two presentations lifts to the presentation site above the covering sieve of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_sieve_spanAt_eq`: above an arrow `b` of that sieve the
restricted presentation `P|_b` maps both to `P`, over `b`, and to `Q`, over `b ≫ h`. -/
theorem isLocallyFull_idealPresForget : (idealPresForget 𝓘).IsLocallyFull X.J where
  functorPushforward_imageSieve_mem {P Q} h := by
    obtain ⟨S, hS, hspan⟩ := exists_sieve_spanAt_eq 𝓘 P Q h
    refine X.J.superset_covering (fun V b hb ↦ ?_) hS
    refine ⟨P.restrict b, P.restrictHom b, 𝟙 V, ⟨?_, (Category.id_comp b).symm⟩⟩
    refine ⟨⟨b ≫ h, fun V' a q hq ↦ ?_⟩, rfl⟩
    exact (P.spanAt_restrict b a).trans <|
      (hspan (a ≫ b) (S.downward_closed hb a)).trans <|
        congrArg (spanAt Q.gen) ((Category.assoc a b h).trans hq)

/-- **The presentation site is a dense subsite of `(𝒞, J)`**, with the topology for which a
sieve covers exactly when its image in `𝒞` does, given a family of objects covering the final
object on each of which `ℐ` is generated by finitely many sections. -/
theorem isDenseSubsite_idealPresForget {ι : Type*} {V : ι → X.C}
    (hV : X.J.CoversTop V) (hfg : ∀ i, IsFinitelyGeneratedOver 𝓘 (V i)) :
    (idealPresForget 𝓘).IsDenseSubsite
      ((idealPresForget 𝓘).restrictedTopology X.J) X.J :=
  let := isCoverDense_idealPresForget 𝓘 hV hfg
  let := isLocallyFull_idealPresForget 𝓘
  inferInstance

end DenseSubsite

section Tautological

open Stacks.RingIdealSite

variable {X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}}
  (𝓘 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))

/-- **The ideal a presentation spans over its own base.** This is the finitely generated ideal
`I ⊆ ℐ(U)` of [Stacks, Tag 099E], read off the chosen generators. -/
def presIdeal (P : IdealPres 𝓘) : Ideal (X.O.obj.obj (op P.obj)) := spanAt P.gen (𝟙 P.obj)

/-- **The tautological functor from the presentation site into the rings with an ideal**: a
presentation goes to its ring of sections together with the ideal it spans there. -/
def idealPresRingIdeal : (IdealPres 𝓘)ᵒᵖ ⥤ RingIdeal.{w} :=
  ofIdealAssignment ((idealPresForget 𝓘).op ⋙ X.O.obj) (fun P ↦ presIdeal 𝓘 P.unop)
    fun {_ _} u ↦
      (u.unop.spanAt_eq (𝟙 _) u.unop.base (Category.id_comp _)).trans
        (spanAt_eq_map_spanAt _ u.unop.base)

/-- The ring of `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealPresRingIdeal` at `P` is the ring of sections
of `𝒪` over the base of `P`. -/
@[simp]
theorem idealPresRingIdeal_obj_ring (P : (IdealPres 𝓘)ᵒᵖ) :
    ((idealPresRingIdeal 𝓘).obj P).ring = X.O.obj.obj (op P.unop.obj) := rfl

/-- The ideal of `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealPresRingIdeal` at `P` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.presIdeal P`. -/
@[simp]
theorem idealPresRingIdeal_obj_ideal (P : (IdealPres 𝓘)ᵒᵖ) :
    ((idealPresRingIdeal 𝓘).obj P).ideal = presIdeal 𝓘 P.unop := rfl

/-- **The pullback of presheaves of modules along
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealPresRingIdeal`.** -/
abbrev idealPresPullback :
    RingIdealModule.{w} ⥤
      PresheafOfModules.{w}
        ((idealPresForget 𝓘).op ⋙ ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj) :=
  PresheafOfModules.pushforward₀ (idealPresRingIdeal 𝓘).rightOp structureRings.{w}

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealPresPullback` preserves zero morphisms. -/
instance preservesZeroMorphisms_idealPresPullback :
    (idealPresPullback 𝓘).PreservesZeroMorphisms where
  map_zero _ _ := PresheafOfModules.hom_ext fun _ ↦ rfl

/-- **The complex `K^•` of [Stacks, Tag 099D] on the presentation site**, as a complex of
presheaves of modules over the restricted structure sheaf: the pullback of
`Stacks.RingIdealSite.kComplexNat` along the tautological functor. Its value at a presentation
`P` is `K(𝒪(P.obj), I_P)`. -/
abbrev presCechComplex :
    CochainComplex
      (PresheafOfModules.{w}
        ((idealPresForget 𝓘).op ⋙ ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj)) ℕ :=
  ((idealPresPullback 𝓘).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℕ)).obj kComplexNat.{w}

/-- **The augmentation of `K^•` onto the restricted structure presheaf.** -/
abbrev presCechAugmentation :
    (presCechComplex 𝓘).X 0 ⟶
      PresheafOfModules.unit
        ((idealPresForget 𝓘).op ⋙ ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj) :=
  (idealPresPullback 𝓘).map kAugZero.{w}

/-- The degree-`n` term of `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.presCechComplex` at a presentation `P` is
the colimit of the Čech term diagram of the ring of sections over `P.obj` and the ideal
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.presIdeal P`. -/
theorem presCechComplex_obj (n : ℕ) (P : (IdealPres 𝓘)ᵒᵖ) :
    ((presCechComplex 𝓘).X n).obj P =
      (colimit (Stacks.GenSetCech.cechTermDiagram (X.O.obj.obj (op P.unop.obj))
        (presIdeal 𝓘 P.unop) n) : ModuleCat.{w} (X.O.obj.obj (op P.unop.obj))) := rfl

end Tautological

section Slice

open Stacks.RingIdealSite

variable {X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}}
  {𝓘 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))}

/-- For a morphism `φ : V ⟶ W` in `𝒞/U` and arrows `a : Z ⟶ V.left`, `q : Z ⟶ W.left` with
`a ≫ φ.left = q`, the composites `a ≫ V.hom` and `q ≫ W.hom` agree. -/
theorem over_comp_hom_eq {U : X.C} {V W : Over U} (φ : V ⟶ W) {Z : X.C}
    {a : Z ⟶ V.left} {q : Z ⟶ W.left} (hq : a ≫ φ.left = q) :
    a ≫ V.hom = q ≫ W.hom := by
  rw [← hq, Category.assoc, Over.w]

/-- **The slice site over the base of a presentation, read inside the presentation site.** An
object `V ⟶ P.obj` of `𝒞/P.obj` goes to the restriction of `P` along it, which is a presentation
with the same number of generators; a morphism goes to its underlying arrow of `𝒞`. -/
def idealPresOver (P : IdealPres 𝓘) : Over P.obj ⥤ IdealPres 𝓘 where
  obj V := P.restrict V.hom
  map {V W} φ :=
    { base := φ.left
      spanAt_eq := fun {_} a q hq ↦
        (P.spanAt_restrict V.hom a).trans
          (Eq.trans (congrArg (spanAt P.gen) (over_comp_hom_eq φ hq))
            (P.spanAt_restrict W.hom q).symm) }
  map_id _ := IdealPres.Hom.ext' rfl
  map_comp _ _ := IdealPres.Hom.ext' rfl

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealPresOver P` sends `V` to the restriction of `P` along
`V.hom`. -/
@[simp]
theorem idealPresOver_obj (P : IdealPres 𝓘) (V : Over P.obj) :
    (idealPresOver P).obj V = P.restrict V.hom := rfl

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealPresOver P` sends a morphism `φ` of `𝒞/P.obj` to a
morphism of presentations with underlying arrow `φ.left`. -/
@[simp]
theorem idealPresOver_map (P : IdealPres 𝓘) {V W : Over P.obj} (φ : V ⟶ W) :
    IdealPres.Hom.base ((idealPresOver P).map φ) = φ.left := rfl

/-- **The slice over `P.obj` sits over the presentation site compatibly with the projections to
`𝒞`**, on the nose: both composites send an object `V ⟶ P.obj` to `V` and a morphism to its
underlying arrow. -/
theorem idealPresOver_comp_forget (P : IdealPres 𝓘) :
    idealPresOver P ⋙ idealPresForget 𝓘 = Over.forget P.obj := rfl

/-- **The tautological functor into the rings with an ideal restricts, along a presentation, to
the one attached to that presentation's generators on the slice site.** -/
theorem idealPresOver_op_comp_idealPresRingIdeal (P : IdealPres 𝓘) :
    (idealPresOver P).op ⋙ idealPresRingIdeal 𝓘 =
      ringIdealFunctor (X := X.over P.obj) P.gen :=
  (comp_ofIdealAssignment ((idealPresForget 𝓘).op ⋙ X.O.obj)
    (idealPresOver P) (fun Q ↦ presIdeal 𝓘 Q.unop)
    (fun {_ _} u ↦ (u.unop.spanAt_eq (𝟙 _) u.unop.base (Category.id_comp _)).trans
      (spanAt_eq_map_spanAt _ u.unop.base))).trans
    (ofIdealAssignment_congr _ _ _
      (funext fun V ↦ congrArg (spanAt P.gen) (Category.id_comp V.unop.hom)))

/-- The composite of `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealPresOver P` with the functor
`(idealPresRingIdeal 𝓘).rightOp` into `RingIdealᵒᵖ` is
`(AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.ringIdealFunctor P.gen).rightOp`. -/
theorem idealPresOver_comp_rightOp (P : IdealPres 𝓘) :
    idealPresOver P ⋙ (idealPresRingIdeal 𝓘).rightOp =
      (ringIdealFunctor (X := X.over P.obj) P.gen).rightOp :=
  congrArg CategoryTheory.Functor.rightOp (idealPresOver_op_comp_idealPresRingIdeal P)

end Slice

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
